.\" dvbrx-web(8): web monitoring page for dvbrx
.TH DVBRX-WEB 8 2026-11-06 "dvbrx 0.1" "dvbrx manual"
.SH NAME
dvbrx-web \- web monitoring interface for dvbrx receivers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY dvbrx\-web
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-socket
.RI [ NAME =] PATH ]...\&
.RB [ \-\-data\-dir
.IR DIRECTORY ]
.YS
.SY dvbrx\-web
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dvbrx-web
serves a web page (port 8099 by default) that talks to the
.BR dvbrx (8)
daemons through their control sockets. Tabs:
.TP
.BR Status " (Statut)"
the radio (device and serial number, USB bus usage, frequency, filter,
rate, gain, AGC, level, estimated power, overflows, LNB) and, per adapter, the
parameters of the received channel (standard, modulation, code rate, SNR, TS
bit rate, errors).
.TP
.B Constellation
the scatter plot of the received channel.
.TP
.BR "Quick scan" " (Scan rapide)"
spectrum by FFT and channel detection (cable/terrestrial, satellite with the
four combinations of the universal LNB).
.TP
.BR "Full scan" " (Scan complet)"
identification of the standard and probing of each channel; export in dvbv5
format for tvheadend.
.TP
.BR Alignment " (Alignement)"
tracking of a satellite carrier or of a DVB-T/T2 multiplex: power, SNR,
lock, history, optional sound. The gain is automatic or fixed: when fixed,
levels compare directly from one antenna position to the next (the AGC no
longer compensates); dvbrx goes back to its own gain when it stops.
.PP
Status and constellation do not take the radio. Scan and alignment take it:
when an application (tvheadend) is using it, dvbrx answers
.B busy
and the page offers to force, which interrupts the current tuning.
.PP
With several receivers, a selector at the top of the page shows them with
their radio (\(lqdvbrx 1 \(em HackRF One 334c64dc39395367\(rq); scans and
alignment are done one receiver at a time.
.PP
There is no authentication: expose the page only to the local network, or
make it listen on 127.0.0.1 behind a proxy that authenticates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Configuration in INI format (commented example:
.IR /etc/dvbrxd/web.conf ).
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " ADDRESS"
Listening address (default 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
HTTP port (default 8099).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " [\fINAME\fR=]\fIPATH\fR"
Socket of a dvbrx daemon (repeatable option). With neither
.B \-\-socket
nor
.B sockets
in the configuration: all the
.I /run/dvbrx/dvbrx\-*.sock
present at startup.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " DIRECTORY"
Scan results (default
.IR /var/lib/dvbrx\-web ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/dvbrxd/web.conf
Configuration: sockets, LNB, inputs, scan ranges and thresholds.
.TP
.B /var/lib/dvbrx-web
Latest quick and full scans of each receiver.
.TP
.B dvbrx-web.service
systemd service, installed but not enabled:
.BR "systemctl enable \-\-now dvbrx\-web" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dvbrx (8),
.BR tvheadend (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/dvbrx-web/README.md, /usr/share/doc/dvbrx/dvbrx-web-api.md
